  "pdf": {
    "title": "Hays Travel Q3 Commercial Margin, MDM & 'Audit Genie' Reconciliation Report (Sunderland HQ)",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "1. Executive Summary & Board '1/3 Vista Mix' Mandate",
        "content": "Across Hays Travel's \u00a33.0B TTV estate (500 retail branches generating 68.44% of bookings and 161 Contact Centre FTEs), shifting short-haul third-party package volume (Jet2holidays 32.91%, easyJet 16.12%, TUI 15.33% at 10-12% commission) into in-house Vista dynamic packages and Cruise-and-Stay itineraries (15-25% gross margin) is our primary profitability lever ahead of the 9 November 2026 Vista Platform launch. However, manual re-keying from supplier extranets into Traveltek iSell has created 292,000 duplicate hotel strings in Azure Databricks Silver and obscured \u00a359M (5.92%) in cancellation exposure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "2. Cross-Source iBOS Commission Variance & 'Audit Genie' Deferral Findings",
        "content": "Reconciliation between supplier settlement statements (external_ledger.xlsx) and Traveltek iBOS expected margin (isell_bookings_inquiries) isolated four critical anomalies totaling \u00a3643.81 in untracked margin variance and \u00a324,940.00 in high-risk transaction value. Specifically, booking HT-884120 (SCV-HH-84920, Henderson Family at Maidenhead Branch MAID-042) exhibits a -12.4% margin discrepancy (\u00a31,406.10 expected in iSell vs \u00a31,231.74 supplier settlement) caused by an unmapped free-text TUI extranet hotel entry ('Riu Palace Adeje Costa (TUI Extranet)'). Additionally, Databricks Audit Genie flagged three bookings (HT-884105, HT-884112, HT-884119) where departure dates were pushed out by exactly 12 months (deferral_months_shifted = 12) while Direct Debit accounts sat in Default_Risk, artificially inflating monthly branch sales bonus attainment."
      }
    ],
